WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING

1. Use it. Download, install and play with this mod, alone or alongside any other
   mods, for as long as you like.

2. Modify your own copy. Change any part of it for your own use, including
   editing prompts, settings and scripts.

3. Publish patches, add-ons and translations that REQUIRE this mod rather than
   containing it. A compatibility patch, a prompt override, an add-on that reads
   this mod's data, a translation of its text — all fine, and none of them needs
   permission. Do not include this mod's own files in your download.

4. Interoperate freely, and without permission. Reading this mod's StorageUtil
   keys, calling its decorators, rendering its prompt submodules, building
   against its documented behaviour, or writing a mod that depends on it are all
   expressly permitted. Interoperating is not copying, and nothing here restricts
   it. Other authors are encouraged to do exactly this.

5. Fork this repository on GitHub in order to prepare a contribution, report a
   bug, or read the history.


WHAT NEEDS PERMISSION FIRST

6. Redistributing this mod, or a substantial part of it, anywhere — including
   Nexus, other mod sites, Discord servers, or your own repository releases.

7. Publishing a modified or rebranded version of this mod.

8. Including this mod in a collection, modpack, compilation or mod list that
   distributes its files rather than linking to them.

Just ask. Permission is usually given, and quickly. The purpose of this clause is
not to hoard the work — it is to keep one canonical version so that users are not
split across divergent copies and so that bug reports mean something.


WHAT IS NOT PERMITTED

9. Commercial use of any kind. This includes selling it, bundling it with
